00:23:50.257 --> 00:23:53.433
- Is there a definite way
to measure fluorescence?

00:23:55.980 --> 00:23:58.660
- Yes, there is a way
to measure fluorescence,

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:02.030
but in my hands I think
you have to be careful

00:24:02.030 --> 00:24:05.540
about measuring fluorescence,

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:10.040
the amount of fluorescence,
you will need to have some kind

00:24:10.040 --> 00:24:13.930
of other tag in your worm,

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:16.830
some other fluorescent tag

00:24:16.830 --> 00:24:19.920
that you will know should
be something constant

00:24:19.920 --> 00:24:23.920
that should not change
from worm to worm too much

00:24:23.920 --> 00:24:26.890
this will be kinda like
your background level

00:24:26.890 --> 00:24:30.030
and if you want to measure any differences

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:32.580
in what you're looking for,
you will be comparing that

00:24:32.580 --> 00:24:35.980
to this kind of background level, to see

00:24:35.980 --> 00:24:38.810
that the variation doesn't come,
just because you're looking

00:24:38.810 --> 00:24:40.930
at different animals,

00:24:40.930 --> 00:24:43.860
they have slightly different age

00:24:43.860 --> 00:24:45.850
may be on different slides

00:24:45.850 --> 00:24:47.430
there is a different fluorescence

00:24:47.430 --> 00:24:49.370
the way that you prepare the slides

00:24:50.380 --> 00:24:55.380
so for me, I prefer not to
measure fluorescence directly,

00:24:55.539 --> 00:24:58.850
I prefer to, you know, when
I look at these structures

00:24:58.850 --> 00:25:02.960
and I see this one GFP
blob, I will say, Oh

00:25:02.960 --> 00:25:06.220
in this cell, I will,
I observe this one blob

00:25:06.220 --> 00:25:09.970
and I will see, do I have any
cells that have two blobs?

00:25:09.970 --> 00:25:11.610
So, then I will count the cells.

00:25:11.610 --> 00:25:14.760
I have 10 cells with one blob

00:25:14.760 --> 00:25:17.320
and I have two cells with two blobs

00:25:17.320 --> 00:25:21.460
and this is the kinda
quantification I prefer to do myself

00:25:21.460 --> 00:25:23.210
but people do measure fluorescence

00:25:23.210 --> 00:25:26.543
you just have to be more
careful how you do it.

00:25:27.720 --> 00:25:32.720
So you don't introduce any
error into your quantification.

00:25:33.090 --> 00:25:35.650
